.TH SAMPLER "9"  "2006-11-18" "LinuxCNC Documentation" "HAL User's Manual"
.SH NAME
sampler \- sample data from HAL in real time
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B loadrt sampler
.RB [ <\fINAME\fR[,\fINAME\fR...]> ]
.BI depth= depth
.BI cfg= string

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sampler
and
.BR halsampler (1)
are used together to sample HAL data in real time and store it in a file.
.B sampler
is a realtime HAL component that exports HAL pins and samples them into a ring
buffer every time its function runs.
.B stmakd
streams the ring to WebSocket clients such as
.BR halsampler ,
which copies it to stdout.  The instance name defaults to \fBsampler\fR.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI depth= depth
sets the number of samples the ring holds, 1000 by default.  The sampler never
waits for its readers: a reader that falls more than
.I depth
samples behind loses the oldest ones.  Every sample on the stream carries its
index, so the client sees each loss and how big it was;
.B halsampler
reports it and exits with failure.  Choose
.I depth
to bridge momentary stalls of the non-realtime side; it costs
.I depth
\(mu 8 bytes per pin.
.TP
.BI cfg= string
defines the set of HAL pins that
.B sampler
exports and later samples data from.
.B sampler
exports one pin for each character in
.I string.
Legal characters are:
.IP "" 7
.B f
(float pin)
.IP "" 7
.B b
(bit pin)
.IP "" 7
.B s
(s32 pin)
.IP "" 7
.B u
(u32 pin)

.SH FUNCTIONS
.TP
.I NAME
Samples the pins into the ring.

.SH PINS
.TP
\fINAME\fB.pin.\fIM\fR input
Pin for the data that will wind up in column
.I M
of the output.  The pin type depends on the config string.
.TP
\fINAME\fB.curr\-depth\fR s32 output
How far the slowest connected reader lags behind, in samples.  When this
reaches
.I depth
that reader starts losing samples.
.TP
\fINAME\fB.full\fR bit output
TRUE while the slowest connected reader lags
.I depth
samples or more.
.TP
\fINAME\fB.enable\fR bit input
When TRUE, samples are captured, when FALSE, no samples are acquired (and none
count as lost).  Defaults to TRUE.
.TP
\fINAME\fB.overruns\fR s32 read/write
Incremented on every function run while
.B full
is TRUE; it counts periods spent full, not samples lost.  Can be reset with
.BR setp .
.TP
\fINAME\fB.sample\-num\fR s32 read/write
Incremented for each sample; can be reset with
.BR setp .
The numbers
.B halsampler \-t
prints come from the stream itself, not from this pin.

.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR halsampler (1),
.BR streamer (9),
.BR halstreamer (1)

